or from ref_image_4 retained as the environment.\n<Audio 1>: fully_copy - <Audio 1> is reused 1:1 as the target video's complete final audio track / background score.\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a live-action cinematic commercial spot in a high-end cold-black aesthetic with 35mm film grain and Kodak Vision3 500T color science, shot on a large-aperture lens with shallow depth of field; morning backlight and dawn sunlight create cold-white contrast with naturally graded light transitions. The entire 15-second film is one continuous, unbroken take executed with machine-arm / motorized-slider precision — absolutely no handheld shake, no cut, no flicker, and no post-transition.\n[Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, the camera opens on a medium close-up inside <Subject 5>, the open office with floor-to-ceiling glass walls opening onto a city skyline where dawn light spills over the horizon; the wet floor after rain throws soft reflective highlights, and strong morning backlight from behind the windows carves clean rim light, halos, and layered silhouettes. From 0.0 to 1.0 seconds, the camera pulls back smoothly with small amplitude at slow speed; dead center is <Subject 1>, the Asian woman from ref_image_0 in her exact referenced outfit, her head tilted slightly downward, then slowly lifting her gaze to open her eyes toward the lens with a calm, restrained expression — the backlight draws a crisp line along her shoulder and the contour of her profile. From 1.0 to 3.0 seconds, the camera keeps pulling back while panning right with small amplitude at slow speed; <Subject 3>, the Asian woman from ref_image_2 in her referenced clothing, enters the frame center horizontally from the right. The focal plane drifts gently onto <Subject 3>'s face as she turns her head to meet the lens, completing a seamless on-camera transition; throughout the occlusion the focus holds perfectly stable — no cut, no black frame. From 3.0 to 8.0 seconds, the camera smoothly dollies out and arcs left (dolly out + arc left), bringing <Subject 2>, the Asian female lead from ref_image_1, into the center; she holds direct eye contact with the lens, calm and confident, and crosses her arms over her chest. The camera then arcs right and pulls back while lowering on a pedestal to a low upward angle, fully revealing the office interior of <Subject 5>; seated in an office swivel chair with arms also crossed is <Subject 4>, the Asian man from ref_image_3, his referenced attire intact, with sunlight streaming from behind him to produce a strong cinematic backlight and halo. From 8.0 to 15.0 seconds, the camera continues to retreat with minimal motion and settles into a stable wide-angle composition that holds as a freeze: the four subjects stand in a front-to-back parallel arrangement — <Subject 2> at front center as the final visual anchor, <Subject 3> to her right, <Subject 1> at the right-rear of <Subject 3>, and <Subject 4> at the left-rear of <Subject 3>. The city skyline and dawn beyond the floor-to-ceiling windows sit in the gaps between the four figures; sunlight, halos, the morning city, and the wet-ground reflections together form a high-end commercial group portrait. The four keep only very subtle, natural micro-movements before the frame locks into a cold, free, modern office tableau. <Audio 1> plays continuously as the complete background score across the whole take. The camera stays perfectly level with a locked horizon throughout — no tilt, no roll, no rotation. The composition is strictly controlled: no extra passersby, no fifth figure, no duplicated or cloned subjects, no facial deformation or copy artifacts, no limb distortion, no background shadow figures, no spatial warping, no stutter or jump, no unexplained background dissolve, no high-speed violent orbit, no overexposure, and no subject is fully swallowed into black by the backlight.\noverall_soundscape:\nA near-silent indoor room tone underlies the take, with only faint fabric rustle as